      "message": "nit: looks like generally in this `pkvm.h` we declare only those functions that are implemented in `pkvm.c` (with a small exception: a few functions implemented in KVM\u0027s `x86.c`, e.g. `pkvm_vcpu_enter_guest()`).\n\nSo, for consistency with other source files, we might declare these functions in a separate `printf.h` header?\n\n...Or maybe an even more consistent approach would be to rename these functions to `vscnprintf()` and `scnprintf()`, so that pKVM can just use the Linux header (`include/linux/sprintf.h`) for their declarations? And then also move `printf.c` into `arch/x86/kvm/pkvm/lib/` ?",
